    description: "FOUND 2026-09-28 while preparing WI-nunab's PR. scripts/check-package-coverage core, run on a pinned worktree of dev at 02c27cad97 (PYTHONPATH to the worktree's packages/*/src), reports ONE line uncovered in core isolation:\n\n    packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/cli.py  6834   the 'continue' in the WI-rusil scoped no-taint-catalogue loop\n        if _tf is None or _tf.source_taint in blind_by_source_taint:\n            continue\n\nIt was introduced by b297d1ce81 (WI-rusil, 2026-09-27). PR CI checks coverage only for a PR's CHANGED files, in a combined run, so it passed there. The same line is uncovered on the WI-nunab branch, which does not touch cli.py. The next PR that edits cli.py will fail its coverage gate on a line it did not write.\n\nFIX: a core test whose claims file mixes a boundary claim (_tf is None) with a taint claim, over a fixture containing a language with no taint catalogue, so the census loop runs and skips the boundary claim. Read test_taint_blind_claim_scope.py first; its fixtures use php + python with taint claims only."  # 8594
